 "findings": {
  "low_level": [
   "Registers 29 to 127 over the 40 distinct kernels behind the card's cells (0 with register spills, a kernel measured in more than one batch counts once), shared memory 1040 to 65600 bytes, harness 0.10 on gb200-nvl4-ts2-99.",
   "Adapter statics: input arrangement packed_rows, output indices, temp storage 1 to 1 bytes, 2 rows per group.",
   "Oracle battery (23 cases per cell plus the measurement seeds) passed on every cell that has a number, 60 cells unsupported by the adapter's contract or the device, no cell failed the oracle."
  ],
  "algorithmic": [
   "Random input (the one-node matrix on gb200-nvl4-ts2-99): throughput not_guaranteed wins 2 of 7 cells (1 as N5_rows_fs_sub@T8, 1 as N5_rows_fs_sub@T16, runner-up in 0), throughput prefer_smaller_index wins 2 of 6 cells (1 as N5_rows_fs_sub@T8, 1 as N5_rows_fs_sub@T16, runner-up in 0).",
   "Where it wins on random input (bf16 N 8, bf16 N 128), the median margin over the runner-up is +40 percent and over the scope's reference control +137 percent.",
   "Largest random-input deficits (distinct cells, worst regime): bf16 N 128 k 4 +174 percent behind W2_packed_sw_v2@T16 in throughput not_guaranteed, bf16 N 32 k 4 +25 percent behind W2_packed_sw_v2@T4 in throughput not_guaranteed, bf16 N 128 k 16 +24 percent behind W2_packed_sw_v2@T8 in throughput not_guaranteed, bf16 N 32 k 16 +14 percent behind W2_packed_sw_v2@T8 in throughput prefer_smaller_index."
  ],
  "negative": [
   "No sorted output by contract (card: sorted_output_support none). Throughput only.",
   "The GB200 pass measured random input only on one host (gb200-nvl4-ts2-99): the tie_heavy, shuffled-tie and phase 3b order-check findings for this adapter are on its B200 card."
  ],
  "surprises": [
   "At N 128 the 16-lane form runs lower in throughput than on B200 (bf16 k 16: 418 against 604 Gelem/s), which moves the cell to W2_packed_sw_v2 at 8 lanes (519 Gelem/s), a generation effect confirmed on a second GB200 host."
  ],
  "open_questions": [
   "B200 pass (WINNERS_b200.md, random input on umbriel-b200-047, tie_heavy on 068, shuffled ties on 094, phase 3b on 047): the warp and sub-warp winners agree with GB200 on 359 of 376 common cells (365 of 376 when each cell is compared through the adapters both passes measured, as section 16 of the knowledge base does), the differences are named sub-warp lane-count cells, N 128 sub-warp throughput cells and warp ties within 5 percent, and in the block matrices the B1_idx against B1_det2 throughput ties fall either way. On GB200 the k 64 cells at 128 threads run 3 to 15 percent slower than on B200 (hw-researcher, a generation property) and the aarch64 cicc emits branches for the conditional swaps (T20, 3 to 4 percent)."
  ]
 },
